@layer base, theme;
@layer base { .title { color: red !important; } }
@layer theme { .title { color: blue !important; } }

Correct Answer:
Important declarations reverse named-layer precedence. Remove important from both declarations to make the later normal theme layer win.

@layer base, theme;
@layer base { .title { color: red; } }
@layer theme { .title { color: blue; } }

